        "An offer to provide this item&#x2014;for example, an offer to sell a product, rent the DVD of a movie, perform a service, or give away tickets to an event. Use [[businessFunction]] to indicate the kind of transaction offered, i.e. sell, lease, etc. This property can also be used to describe a [[Demand]]. While this property is listed as expected on a number of common types, it can be used in others. In that case, using a second type, such as Product or a subtype of Product, can clarify the nature of the offer.",
  )
  $SchemaUnion? get offers;

  /// An organizer of an Event.
  @Schema(description: "An organizer of an Event.")
  $SchemaUnion? get organizer;

  /// A performer at the event&#x2014;for example, a presenter, musician, musical group or actor.
  @Schema(
    description:
        "A performer at the event&#x2014;for example, a presenter, musician, musical group or actor.",
  )
  $SchemaUnion? get performer;

  /// The main performer or performers of the event&#x2014;for example, a presenter, musician, or actor.
  @Schema(
    description:
        "The main performer or performers of the event&#x2014;for example, a presenter, musician, or actor.",
  )
  $SchemaUnion? get performers;

  /// Used in conjunction with eventStatus for rescheduled or cancelled events. This property contains the previously scheduled start date. For rescheduled events, the startDate property should be used for the newly scheduled start date. In the (rare) case of an event that has been postponed and rescheduled multiple times, this field may be repeated.
  @Schema(
    description:
        "Used in conjunction with eventStatus for rescheduled or cancelled events. This property contains the previously scheduled start date. For rescheduled events, the startDate property should be used for the newly scheduled start date. In the (rare) case of an event that has been postponed and rescheduled multiple times, this field may be repeated.",
  )
  $SchemaUnion? get previousStartDate;

  /// The CreativeWork that captured all or part of this Event.
  @Schema(
    description: "The CreativeWork that captured all or part of this Event.",
  )
  $CreativeWork? get recordedIn;

  /// The number of attendee places for an event that remain unallocated.
  @Schema(
    description:
        "The number of attendee places for an event that remain unallocated.",
  )
  num? get remainingAttendeeCapacity;

  /// A review of the item.
  @Schema(description: "A review of the item.")
  $Review? get review;

  /// A person or organization that supports a thing through a pledge, promise, or financial contribution. E.g. a sponsor of a Medical Study or a corporate sponsor of an event.
  @Schema(
    description:
        "A person or organization that supports a thing through a pledge, promise, or financial contribution. E.g. a sponsor of a Medical Study or a corporate sponsor of an event.",
  )
  $SchemaUnion? get sponsor;

  /// The start date and time of the item (in [ISO 8601 date format](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601)).
  @Schema(
    description:
        "The start date and time of the item (in [ISO 8601 date format](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601)).",
  )
  $SchemaUnion? get startDate;

  /// An Event that is part of this event. For example, a conference event includes many presentations, each of which is a subEvent of the conference.
  @Schema(
    description:
        "An Event that is part of this event. For example, a conference event includes many presentations, each of which is a subEvent of the conference.",
  )
  $Event? get subEvent;

  /// Events that are a part of this event. For example, a conference event includes many presentations, each subEvents of the conference.
  @Schema(
    description:
        "Events that are a part of this event. For example, a conference event includes many presentations, each subEvents of the conference.",
  )
  $Event? get subEvents;

  /// An event that this event is a part of. For example, a collection of individual music performances might each have a music festival as their superEvent.
  @Schema(
    description:
        "An event that this event is a part of. For example, a collection of individual music performances might each have a music festival as their superEvent.",
  )
  $Event? get superEvent;

  /// Organization or person who adapts a creative work to different languages, regional differences and technical requirements of a target market, or that translates during some event.
  @Schema(
    description:
        "Organization or person who adapts a creative work to different languages, regional differences and technical requirements of a target market, or that translates during some event.",
  )
  $SchemaUnion? get translator;

  /// The typical expected age range, e.g. '7-9', '11-'.
  @Schema(description: "The typical expected age range, e.g. '7-9', '11-'.")
  String? get typicalAgeRange;

  /// A work featured in some event, e.g. exhibited in an ExhibitionEvent.        Specific subproperties are available for workPerformed (e.g. a play), or a workPresented (a Movie at a ScreeningEvent).
  @Schema(
    description:
        "A work featured in some event, e.g. exhibited in an ExhibitionEvent.        Specific subproperties are available for workPerformed (e.g. a play), or a workPresented (a Movie at a ScreeningEvent).",
  )
  $CreativeWork? get workFeatured;

  /// A work performed in some event, for example a play performed in a TheaterEvent.
  @Schema(
    description:
        "A work performed in some event, for example a play performed in a TheaterEvent.",
  )
  $CreativeWork? get workPerformed;
}

